  data: {
    LLM: "Only bid if you have a strong hand. A good Suit hand needs 5+ trumps including top Jacks. A Grand hand needs 2-3 top Jacks and side Aces. In Null, you need 7s, 8s, 9s in every suit or voids. As a Defender, lead a suit the Soloist is likely void in (long suit) to force a trump, or lead trumps if the Soloist is weak in them (to drain them).\n\nThe 'Short Suit' Lead: Against a Suit game, lead a short suit (singleton/doubleton) to try to ruff. But be careful not to free up the Soloist's losers.\n\nCounting Matadors: If you have the Jack of Spades (2nd highest) but not the Jack of Clubs, you are 'Without 1'. Game Value = (1+1) * Base. If you pick up the Jack of Clubs from the Skat, you are now 'With 2' (J-Clubs, J-Spades). This changes your multiplier from 2 to 3. Be wary of overbidding if you rely on the Skat.",
    Player: "Only bid if you have a strong hand. A good Suit hand needs 5+ trumps including top Jacks. A Grand hand needs 2-3 top Jacks and side Aces. In Null, you need 7s, 8s, 9s in every suit or voids. As a Defender, lead a suit the Soloist is likely void in (long suit) to force a trump, or lead trumps if the Soloist is weak in them (to drain them).\n\nThe 'Short Suit' Lead: Against a Suit game, lead a short suit (singleton/doubleton) to try to ruff. But be careful not to free up the Soloist's losers.\n\nCounting Matadors: If you have the Jack of Spades (2nd highest) but not the Jack of Clubs, you are 'Without 1'. Game Value = (1+1) * Base. If you pick up the Jack of Clubs from the Skat, you are now 'With 2' (J-Clubs, J-Spades). This changes your multiplier from 2 to 3. Be wary of overbidding if you rely on the Skat.",
